1.2.x series, and we've had problems upgrading our libpng version for Chrome OS, so we've pinned libpng to &lt;1.3. This causes conflicts with the current dependencies for ghostscript.  The ghostscript sources and docs never mention requiring libpng &gt;= 1.6.2, and I have several Ubuntu systems that have ghostscript linked just fine against libpng-1.2.x, so I don't believe it's a technical limitation. And now, I can build and run ghostscript just fine, AFAICT.  It appears, then, that the dependency was chosen for the upstream ebuild was arbitrary, so let's change this to &gt;=1.2.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47758,chrome-os-partner:49267 TEST=`emerge-${BOARD} ghostscript-gpl` works without unmasking &gt;=libpng-1.3 TEST=run CUPS + a few PostScript printers  Change-Id: I6e25d67178bc57b984e9ed0decf8de94e45a4ca5 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322293 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322293" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/93/322293/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idebc09f27028189101f37d27f23e05637eef7e8e" commit="717ff17870a0bac6f7f519e1ec3ccd9a0254fe55" commit_message="coreboot: use SYSTEM_OEM to update mainboard vendor  Use SYSTEM_OEM variable to override mainboard vendor if needed.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49367 BRANCH=firmware-strago-7287.B TEST=Compiled, verified Signed-off-by: Ted Kuo &lt;tedkuo@ami.com.tw&gt;  Change-Id: Idebc09f27028189101f37d27f23e05637eef7e8e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321986 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0"