rd aware submission logic. One of the submit partial pool logics we have now: each project can specify a list of stages it does not care about in its COMMIT-QUEUE.ini file. Changes to that project will be submitted even if those stages fail.  Add another check after this logic: if unignored fail stage is only HWTestStage, submit changes that are unrelated to that failed hardware subsystems.  BUG=chromium:559303 TEST=unittest and tryjob  Change-Id: Ie72cb4735139df790b43085fca3a62c08b0caccf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313740 Commit-Ready: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313740" owner_email="shuqianz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/40/313740/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ic53faa03e4d48cd5ff6fbbfc79c5de8e5c9187b4" commit="6f9a7be53df4dd61fc57e090f480f935a5b8089e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath: Add ATH_DEFER_EEPROM_REGULATORY option  Add option to disable the internal regulatory mask sourced from EEPROM data.  This does not affect CRDA regulatory operation, but nevertheless this option should not be used by default.  This ports CL:49176 from kernel 3.4 to kernel 3.14 (wireless-3.18).  Signed-off-by: mukesh agrawal &lt;quiche@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:575803 TEST=Recompile with new config option enabled and disabled. Ensure that &quot;iw phy&quot; output is as expected in both cases.  Change-Id: Ic53faa03e4d48cd5ff6fbbfc79c5de8e5c9187b4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321726 Commit-Ready: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: mukesh agrawal &lt;quiche@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Stewart &lt;pstew@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler